SPRINT: Seed Catalogue Data into Sanity Content Lake
=====================================================

GOAL: Populate the empty Sanity Studio Catalogue singleton with the full
      recursive tree from catalogue-nav-data.json so it renders correctly
      in Studio and is queryable by the frontend.

ROOT CAUSE OF FAILURE (established):
  - The previous attempt treated Sanity like a file upload target.
  - Sanity Content Lake is a document database. It requires:
      1. A document targeted by its exact _id
      2. Every array item to have a unique _key string
      3. Every object to declare its _type (matching the schema name)
      4. Slug objects to carry _type: "slug"
  - None of those were present in the raw catalogue-nav-data.json payload.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SCOPE 1 — Schema Contract Audit
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Purpose: Confirm the exact field names and types the Sanity schema
         requires before transforming any data.

DoD:
  [ ] Confirmed root document type name:       "catalogue"
  [ ] Confirmed root document singleton _id:   "catalogue"
        (Sanity singletons use the type name as their _id by convention;
         verified via build-catalogue-index.mjs line:
         `*[_id == "catalogue"][0].catalogue`)
  [ ] Confirmed root array field name:         "catalogue"
  [ ] Confirmed object type name:              "catalogueItem"
  [ ] Confirmed object fields and their types:
        title    → string   (required)
        type     → string   ("link" | "header")
        slug     → slug     (_type: "slug", .current: string)
        icon     → string   (optional)
        children → array of catalogueItem (optional)
  [ ] Confirmed that header items with no slug in source data
      are valid (schema hides slug when type === "header",
      so slug may be omitted entirely for headers)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SCOPE 2 — Payload Transformation
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Purpose: Convert the raw catalogue-nav-data.json into a shape that
         satisfies every Sanity database constraint.

DoD:
  [ ] Every node at every depth has _type: "catalogueItem"
  [ ] Every node that appears inside an array has a _key that is:
        - a non-empty string
        - unique across the entire document (not just its sibling array)
  [ ] Slug objects carry _type: "slug" (already present in source;
      must be preserved exactly)
  [ ] Header nodes that lack a slug in the source have slug field omitted
      entirely (not set to null or {}) — Sanity validation ignores
      hidden fields but null slug objects can cause Studio render errors
  [ ] Transformation is pure (no mutation of original JSON)
  [ ] Transformation is recursive (handles arbitrary nesting depth)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SCOPE 3 — Sanity Client Connection
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Purpose: Establish an authenticated write connection to the project.

DoD:
  [ ] Client reads projectId from NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID (.env)
  [ ] Client reads dataset from NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET (.env)
  [ ] Client uses useCdn: false (mutations require direct API)
  [ ] Client uses a SANITY_API_TOKEN with "Editor" or "Deploy Studio"
      write permissions — loaded from SANITY_API_TOKEN in .env
      (this token is NEVER committed to the repo)
  [ ] apiVersion pinned to "2024-11-14" (matches sanity/env.ts)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SCOPE 4 — Database Mutation
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Purpose: Write the transformed payload into the singleton document.

Strategy: createOrReplace (not patch.set) — this is safer for a
  singleton seed because:
    - patch.set fails if the document does not yet exist
    - createOrReplace is idempotent: safe to re-run
    - It sets _id and _type explicitly, satisfying Sanity's
      document-level requirements

DoD:
  [ ] Mutation targets _id: "catalogue", _type: "catalogue"
  [ ] The "catalogue" field is set to the fully transformed array
  [ ] Transaction is committed with { autoGenerateArrayKeys: false }
      (we supply our own _key values; letting Sanity auto-generate
       would create a mismatch if the script is re-run)
  [ ] Script exits with code 0 on success, non-zero on any error
  [ ] Success log prints the count of top-level items written

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SCOPE 5 — Verification
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Purpose: Confirm the data landed correctly before closing the sprint.

DoD:
  [ ] After mutation, script performs a read-back query:
        *[_id == "catalogue"][0].catalogue
      and logs the count of items returned
  [ ] Count matches expected top-level items (3: Headphones,
      Audio Electronics, Accessories)
  [ ] Manual check: reload localhost:3000/studio/structure/catalogue
      → Catalogue array shows 3 root items, each expandable
  [ ] Studio "Publish" button is clicked to promote Draft → Published
      so the frontend GROQ queries (which target published documents
      by default) can resolve the data

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
EXECUTION ORDER
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  1. Add SANITY_API_TOKEN to .env (get from sanity.io/manage → API → Tokens)
  2. Run: node scripts/seed-catalogue.mjs
  3. Check terminal output for success confirmation
  4. Reload Sanity Studio → verify tree renders
  5. Click Publish in Studio
  6. Run: node scripts/build-catalogue-index.mjs
     (rebuilds data/catalogue-index.json from the live Sanity data)
